WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:01.950
Here's what a rule looks like as code.

2
00:00:01.950 --> 00:00:06.527
Each group is one small file: a name,
whether it holds users or devices,

3
00:00:06.527 --> 00:00:11.920
an owner who approves changes, a flag saying
whether it's critical in an incident,

4
00:00:11.920 --> 00:00:15.925
the rule itself with its two guards
at the top, and a few tests.

5
00:00:15.925 --> 00:00:20.853
The tests name people in a fictional
population built to trip every guard:

6
00:00:20.853 --> 00:00:24.730
someone disabled, a guest who
copied an organization code,

7
00:00:24.730 --> 00:00:27.800
a worker with an empty
type, a code in lower case.

8
00:00:27.800 --> 00:00:31.800
If the rule ever lets the wrong
person in, a test says so.
